! Example initial-conditions namelist demonstrating the true force-free
! Bessel-Riccati eigenmode ('force_free_bessel' tag,
! src/core/initial_conditions.f90 + src/core/force_free_bessel.f90,
! 2026-10-15), ROADMAP.md programming task 4's completion. Usable with
! app/mhdvsh_hall_crust_profile.f90's optional ic_namelist_path argument
! (8th CLI arg) exactly like data/ic/bessel_riccati_example.nml.
!
! Unlike 'bessel_riccati' (arbitrary, user-picked A/B/X_SCALE -- not
! generally BC-consistent), this tag SOLVES for the eigenvalue mu_l and
! the Riccati-Bessel mix (a,b) satisfying curl(B)=mu_l*B at degree l,
! subject to Phi(R_min)=Phi(R_max)=0 exactly (hence Psi(R_min)=Psi(R_max)
! =0 too, via the force-free coupling Psi_l(r)=-mu_l*Phi_l(r)). Per user
! decision 2026-10-15: this prioritizes the exact Dirichlet BCs over the
! outer Robin (vacuum-decay) condition -- see force_free_bessel.f90's own
! header for the full derivation and the disclosed trade-off (the
! resulting exterior vacuum potential is not guaranteed to decay).
!
! Each mode is (L,M,ROOT_INDEX,AMPLITUDE,OUTER_BC): ROOT_INDEX selects
! which eigenvalue (1=smallest/"fundamental"); AMPLITUDE scales the
! Riccati-Bessel a-coefficient directly (b is fixed by the inner BC, not
! independently settable). Unlike 'bessel_riccati', each mode ALWAYS
! contributes to both Phi and Psi together -- there is no MODE_FIELD.
!
! FF_MODE_OUTER_BC (2026-10-15) picks which outer condition the
! eigenvalue is solved against -- this project's real outer BC
! (Robin(Phi)+Dirichlet(Psi)=0) can't both be satisfied exactly once the
! force-free coupling slaves Psi to Phi (see force_free_bessel.f90's own
! header for the full derivation of both):
!   'double_dirichlet' (this file): forces Phi(R_out)=0, hence B_r(R_out)
!     =0 too -- a special case, not the generic multipole with a nonzero
!     surface field. See force_free_bessel_arbitrary_value_example.nml
!     for the other case (nonzero B_r at the surface).
!   'arbitrary_value': normalizes Phi(R_out) to an arbitrary nonzero
!     value instead (the paper's own Eqs. A17-A19 scheme) -- the
!     physically typical nonzero-B_r-at-the-surface case.
&IC_SELECT
  N_TAGS = 1
  TAGS   = 'force_free_bessel'
/

&FORCE_FREE_BESSEL_MODES
  N_FF_MODES          = 1
  FF_MODE_L           = 1
  FF_MODE_M           = 0
  FF_MODE_ROOT_INDEX  = 1
  FF_MODE_AMPLITUDE   = 1.0
  FF_MODE_OUTER_BC    = 'double_dirichlet'
/
